<title>UK: Copper concentrate ship refloated off Nova Scotia.</title>
<headline>Copper concentrate ship refloated off Nova Scotia.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Panama-flagged bulker Ypapadi has been refloated off Nova Scotia, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Monday.</p>
<p>The 30,330 dwt vessel, carrying 2,500 tonnes of copper concentrate, grounded on December 7 on sand around Latitude 48 51N, Longtitude 64 25.2W.</p>
<p>It was not thought to have not sustained any damage but an inspection is to be performed on December 16, after which it is expected to head for Gaspe, Nova Scotia.</p>
</text>
